event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dev-d002.md\", \"content\": \"Dispatch d002 for dev.\\n\\nImplement the following in your ~/subject repository clone, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. Create `src/greet.py` with a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. Create `tests/test_greet.py` with unit tests covering:\\n   - A normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - The empty string (e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` from the repo root and confirm\\n   it exits 0 (all tests pass). Fix anything necessary until it does.\\n\\n4. Commit your work to your own branch.\\n\\n5. Reply to this dispatch (`cs-campaign-member reply --file \u003cpath\u003e`) with an\\n   honest summary: what you implemented, the exact test command you ran, its\\n   output/exit code, and confirmation that you committed to your branch.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

